<div>
  <h2>The Challenge</h2>

  <div class="side-by-side">
    <div>
      <p class="big">
        {{ subtitle }}
      </p>
    </div>
    <p>
      The Army National Guard needed a strong esports identity for its Code
      Freedom tournament series, which spanned Apex Legends and Counter-Strike
      2. Gaming icons like ImperialHal, iiTzTimmy and Summit1G were taking part,
      so the branding had to do three things:
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="side-by-side">
    <p>
      1. Set Code Freedom apart from other esports circuits with a brand that
      FPS and Battle Royale audiences would respond to.
    </p>
    <p>
      2. Create assets that adapt to multiple tournament cycles and marketing
      campaigns while following the US Army's strict brand guidelines.
    </p>
    <p>
      3. Appeal to both competitive players and casual viewers, and keep the
      brand visible for the whole campaign.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

