<div>
  <h2>The Solution</h2>

  <div class="side-by-side">
    <p class="big">Six Tournaments, Six Looks</p>
    <p>
      I treated each tournament as its own brand instead of one ongoing event.
      Each had fresh visuals, and the series stayed consistent.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="side-by-side">
    <p class="big">Expanding the Guard's Brand Rules</p>
    <p>
      At first the Guard could only approve plain white backgrounds, which
      limited the creative. I wrote design proposals that convinced them to
      widen their branding approach, and the campaign looked far more dynamic as
      a result. It took persuading, and it worked out well for everyone
      involved.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="side-by-side">
    <p class="big">Event Trailers</p>
    <p>
      I directed six event trailers. Each has its own visual identity, and all
      share a high-energy esports look. I treated the Code Freedom logo reveal
      as a film moment so the brand would feel like a franchise, then developed
      a separate trailer concept for each of the six events.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="side-by-side">
  <div>
    <p class="big">Revealing the Code Freedom Style</p>
    <p>
      I directed the reveal trailer that introduced Code Freedom. It centers on
      a 3D recreation of the emblem-style logo lit in gold against a fiery
      backdrop.
    </p>
    <p>
      The trailer shows the logo's individual elements up close. It was Code
      Freedom's first message in 2024 and teased the upcoming events for the
      Apex Legends and Counter-Strike communities.
    </p>
  </div>
